Z||000000||count_iblis||10-09-2000||04:10 PM||||im wondering what is the most easy way to ship a car from kentuck to cali?  how much will this run?||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||10-09-2000||05:08 PM||||Back i June, I had a car shipped from Sacremento, CA to Tampa, FL and it cost me about $1,000. I called around and all carriers were about the same. I used "Expert Auto Transport" and WOULD NOT recommend them. They picked up the car a week late and after it left CA it took almost two weeks to get here. Basically, they lied to me to get my business. Maybe someone else has one they can recommend. Any military people out there that can help?<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||10-09-2000||10:13 PM||||I asked aroung at my local Mr.Goodwrench and they gave me recommendations.  He was a local guy who hauls snowbird cars from upstate NY to Florida.  Trucking 2 Fieros to Twin Lakes from my house was $1300.  Sounds a lot but it was a two day trip one way along toll roads in a diesel flatbed.  I figure the trip was under 1500 miles both ways and he came back empty.  So you figure his time, milage, tolls, food, motel, it was less than a buck a mile. I could have gotten a break if he had something to carry back..  He delivered the cars within 3 days from when he picked them up. This guy had retired and started with local auto dealers hauling cars for them.  Demand came so great he goes all over the country shuffling cars around.  He has 2 ten car haulers in his fleet.   I must have gotten him on a slow week.||||reg||7
